Airbnb Price Analysis and Prediction.
A Python data analysis and machine learning project using the New York City Airbnb Open Data (2019) dataset. This repository contains two Jupyter notebooks that explore Airbnb listing data and build a Linear Regression model to predict listing prices.
Project Overview
The project is organized into two notebooks:
- Notebook 1 — Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA): Examines the dataset structure, data types, missing values, descriptive statistics, duplicate records, and numerical outliers. It also demonstrates price outlier capping and prepares features for analysis.
- Notebook 2 — Airbnb Price Prediction: Preprocesses the data, encodes categorical variables, splits the data into training and testing sets, trains a Linear Regression model, and evaluates its predictions.
Objectives
- Understand the structure and characteristics of NYC Airbnb listings.
- Identify missing values and inspect potential outliers.
- Explore listing attributes such as room type, location, minimum nights, reviews, availability, and price.
- Prepare data for machine learning.
- Train a Linear Regression model to estimate listing prices.
- Evaluate model performance using standard regression metrics and visualizations.
Dataset
The project uses the AB_NYC_2019 dataset, containing Airbnb listings in New York City.
- Records: 48,895
- Original columns: 16
- Target variable: price
- Examples of features: latitude, longitude, room type, neighbourhood, minimum nights, number of reviews, reviews per month, host listing count, and availability.
The dataset includes listing information and host-related attributes. Ensure the dataset file is available in the location referenced by each notebook before running the code.
